aim is strongly implausible or conflicts with remembered facts, set conflict=uncertain and never invent a textual counter source. Keep role fit separate: direct relation claims can be factually false. Do not reject unfamiliar but explicitly supported namesakes just because memory knows only a famous one. A claimed convention secretly being a space agency deserves scrutiny. Do not label same-role competing dates wrong_argument.\nInput: {\"question\": \"What is the medium of \\\"The Man Who Never Was\\\"?\", \"slot_hint\": \"other\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0017-989c4321a69b:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 190, \"text\": \"The Man Who Never Was The Man Who Never Was is a 1956 UK Second World War film, produced by André Hakim, directed by Ronald Neame, that stars Clifton Webb, Gloria Grahame and Robert Flemyng.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0017-989c4321a69b:d00\", \"start\": 191, \"end\": 238, \"text\": \"It is based on the book of the same name by Lt.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0017-989c4321a69b:d00\", \"start\": 239, \"end\": 244, \"text\": \"Cmdr.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0017-989c4321a69b:d00\", \"start\": 245, \"end\": 287, \"text\": \"Ewen Montagu and dramatises actual events.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0017-989c4321a69b:d00\", \"start\": 288, \"end\": 511, \"text\": \"The film's storyline concerns Operation Mincemeat, a 1943 British Intelligence plan to deceive the Axis powers into thinking Operation \\\"Husky\\\", the Allied invasion of Sicily, would take place elsewhere in the Mediterranean.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0017-989c4321a69b:d00\", \"start\": 512, \"end\": 583, \"text\": \"\\\"The Man Who Never Was\\\" was entered into the 1956 Cannes Film Festival.\"}, \"D1S7\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0017-989c4321a69b:d00\", \"start\": 584, \"end\": 589, \"text\": \"Nigel\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0017-989c4321a69b:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 478, \"text\": \"`` A Little Ignorance '' John Newland Merwin Gerard October 19 , 1966 ( 1966-10-19 ) 1209 8 `` Target : Eva '' Walter Doniger Story by : Edmund Morris Teleplay by : William Bast & Edmund Morris October 26 , 1966 ( 1966-10-26 ) 1210 9 `` The Big Fish '' John Newland Donald James November 2 , 1966 ( 1966-11-2 ) 1206 10 `` Pay Now , Pray Later '' John Newland Dick Carr November 9 , 1966 ( 1966-11-9 ) 1211 11 `` Games of Death '' John Newland Story by : Lewis Pine Teleplay by :\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0017-989c4321a69b:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0017-989c4321a69b:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"The Man Who Never Was\", \"scope\": \"1956 UK Second World War film\", \"claim\": \"The Man Who Never Was is a 1956 UK Second World War film.\", \"answer\": \"film\", \"quote\": \"The Man Who Never Was The Man Who Never Was is a 1956 UK Second World War film, produced by André Hakim, directed by Ronald Neame, that stars Clifton Webb, Gloria Grahame and Robert Flemyng.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}], \"R5_answers\": [\"film\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"film\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}]}"
